#### 3. Exactly-Once Semantics (TRANSACTIONAL)

**Configuration:**
```properties
acks=all                  # Wait for all in-sync replicas
enable.idempotence=true   # Prevent duplicates
transactional.id=unique-producer-id  # Enable Kafka transactions
```

**Behavior:**
- Producer sends events within Kafka transactions (begin, commit, abort)
- All events in transaction written atomically (all succeed or all fail)
- Consumers with `isolation.level=read_committed` only see committed events
- Survives producer crashes and restarts without duplicates
- Higher latency (~100-300ms) due to transaction coordination overhead

**Use Case:** Financial transactions (payments, refunds, chargebacks) where duplicates cause business impact

**RECOMMENDED FOR:** Payment processing, financial reconciliation, multi-event atomic operations

**Example:**
```java
// Publish multiple related events atomically
kafkaProducer.beginTransaction();
try {
    kafkaProducer.send("payments.authorized", paymentAuth);
    kafkaProducer.send("accounts.debited", accountDebit);
    kafkaProducer.send("claims.paid", claimPayment);
    kafkaProducer.commitTransaction();  // All 3 events written atomically
} catch (Exception e) {
    kafkaProducer.abortTransaction();  // All 3 events discarded
}
```

